{"id": "EUVD-2026-81871", "enisaUuid": "ad367ca1-65ea-331c-89b1-d9b536e7e30e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd: wait for behind writes before destroying bitmap\n\n__md_stop() destroyed the bitmap before calling mddev_detach(). That made\nmddev_detach() skip bitmap_ops->wait_behind_writes(), because the bitmap\nwas already disconnected from mddev.\n\nThis was still safe for the legacy bitmap because bitmap_destroy() waits\nfor behind writes itself. llbitmap keeps that wait in its\n->wait_behind_writes() operation instead, while ->destroy() tears down the\nllbitmap storage. With the old ordering, RAID1 behind-write completions\ncould still run after llbitmap storage had been freed.\n\nCall mddev_detach() before md_bitmap_destroy() so the common detach path\ncan wait for behind writes while the bitmap is still alive. Only destroy\nthe bitmap after those users are gone.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/73881ff7a75913f919a1ce9d9571bfaab8e8588d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4224dccd325a9380e8edfb66aad8bb5771c94222", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a79365b2278f16e163e4024086105693b421601"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90278", "GHSA-2jp5-w8mw-wp2x"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "215daac7-5add-3a61-807a-011bbaf876d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "43091e60-085b-3200-b6db-947051fe9346", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ab829f1971dc99f2aac10846c378e67fc875abc <4224dccd325a9380e8edfb66aad8bb5771c94222"}, {"id": "85a61cb8-fa00-316d-9a2a-149bd9193d4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "aca61374-6196-3f03-944b-a9955215e5a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ab829f1971dc99f2aac10846c378e67fc875abc <2a79365b2278f16e163e4024086105693b421601"}, {"id": "b9b751ec-48c6-3b36-8852-601c65c203b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "bdf992cd-1118-3a65-a088-006e1eb77c9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "d73ffb00-88ea-363e-a21a-94093a63addf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "f8c14141-c67e-3246-9344-64aa675b1a47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ab829f1971dc99f2aac10846c378e67fc875abc <73881ff7a75913f919a1ce9d9571bfaab8e8588d"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "78a86e38-56be-3169-9480-4ac2dc96fc52", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}